  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe whole-program post took the End-units word from the active setup. Setups could differ in End units since #1535, and the post did not refuse that.\n\nNow `setup_post_options::program_problems` compares the End units too, together with the Output and the thread output. A program with a setup whose End units differ from the active setup's End units is refused by name. The refusal names each option that differs, for example:\n\n```\nsetup 'Setup1' posts with other post options (end units) than the active setup 'Setup2' - post the setups one at a time\n```\n\nThe old text `(output or threading)` is now the list of the options that really differ, for example `(output, end units)`.\n\n## Agreement with the #902 rule\n\nThe program unit (G20 / G21 at the start, and every coordinate) is still the document's one mm / inch setting. It comes from `posting_units::program_options` as `postOptions.Units`. This change does not touch it. No machine file, post, setup or operation chooses it.\n\nEnd units is a post option: the unit mode that the program leaves the control in at the end (#596). After this change, the program also has only one End-units word. All setups must agree on it, so the word never comes from \"whichever setup is active\". The decision file `docs/decisions/1540-end-units-refusal.md` records the alternatives (a documented \"first setup\" rule, a document-only End units) and why they were dropped.\n\n## Posted output\n\nNo change for a program that posts today with agreeing setups, and no change for a single-setup document. A program with setups that differ in End units now refuses the post. Before, it posted with the active setup's word. No golden changed.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New pinning test: `setups_disagreeing_on_the_end_units_are_refused_by_name` in `crates/app/tests/setup_post_options.rs`. It checks the refusal with each setup active, a setup that follows the document, agreement (the same program as the document's own choice), and two differences named together.\n- Mutation check: with the End-units comparison disabled, the new test fails at its first refusal assert. The comparison was then restored.\n- The whole `setup_post_options` suite passes (11 tests), including `setups_disagreeing_on_the_output_are_refused_by_name`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green, 0 failed (app suites, 10.2 min wall). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --test setup_post_options -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real control ran a posted program.\n- The GUI was not launched. The refusal text reaches the GUI through the same verification gate as the Output refusal.\n\nChangelog: The whole-program post refuses by name when setups differ in End units, as it does for the Output and the thread output (#1540)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1540\n",
